### What I saw

Nearly every Release 13 failure traces to four causes: (A) one fact with several owners (models root, declaration shape, input names, paid limits, project); (B) contracts checked only at run time, on a rented GPU; (C) typed facts flattened at a boundary, so waits and failures are invisible; (D) no single table of end states, so "clean up" means "destroy". This is evidence for F-008's and F-003's Current state at their next reassessment, and a test to apply to any plan on the generation path.

Source: Fable deep-cause synthesis, decision log 12 Nov 14:43 UTC (interim file `observations/2026-11-12-four-deep-causes-of-generation-failures.md`, 2026-11-12)

